  "question": {
    "text": "$\\int_{-3 \\pi / 2}^{-\\pi / 2}\\left[(x+\\pi)^3+\\cos ^2(x+3 \\pi)\\right] d x$ is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi^4}{32}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi^4}{32}+\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{4}-1$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\nI=\\int_{-3 \\pi / 2}^{-\\pi / 2}\\left[(x+\\pi)^3+\\cos ^2(x+3 \\pi)\\right] d x\n$$\nPut $\\mathrm{x}+\\pi=\\mathrm{t}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& I=\\int_{-\\pi / 2}^{\\pi / 2}\\left[t^3+\\cos ^2 t\\right] d t=2 \\int_0^{\\pi / 2} \\cos ^2 t d t \\\\\n& =\\int_0^{\\pi / 2}(1+\\cos 2 t) d t=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+0 .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
